From 59619bbdfaf8f00e793323c1695da0035658a7ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 10:43:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/25] harden: 2nd-wave fixes for network-reachable ASUS
 daemons (Tier 1+2)

Second audit pass over ASUS-authored userspace that ships in the RT-BE96U
image but was outside the first audit (httpd/rc/shared/libdisk). Findings
reachability-triaged against config_rt-be96u + the built rootfs + rc start
paths; only in-build, reachable issues fixed here.

Tier 1 - root command/config injection (libovpn, same class as the IPsec fixes):
- openvpn_control.c ovpn_client_up_handler(): the OpenVPN client up/route-up
  handler runs as root and built `ip route ...` strings with system() from
  env vars the REMOTE VPN SERVER controls (route_network/netmask/gateway/
  metric_%d, trusted_ip, route_net_gateway, route_vpn_gateway, dev). Replace
  system() with eval() argv exec and validate every token (inet_pton for IPs,
  strict-numeric metric, alnum dev). Pushed foreign-option DOMAIN is now
  charset-validated before it is written into the dnsmasq config (was a
  newline-injection into a root daemon's config).
- openvpn_setup.c update_ovpn_profie_remote(): sed+system() with the DDNS
  hostname (nvram ddns_hostname_x/_username_x); substitute a safe placeholder
  unless the address is a clean host/IP.
- openvpn_setup.c: verify-x509-name (nvram cn) now rejected if it contains
  quote/backslash/newline (config-directive injection -> script-security/up);
  ccd_val client name validated against path traversal and its addr/netmask
  required to be clean IPv4 before becoming route/iroute directives.

Tier 2 - memory safety in network-listening daemons:
- snooper/igmp.c accept_igmp(): bound the IP header-length advance (ip_hl) so
  the unsigned (end-ptr) length can't underflow past every size check; bound
  the IGMPv3 group-record walk (attacker nsrcs/auxwords) against packet end.
- urlfilterd/filter.c: thread the captured length into updateOffset(), bound
  the IPv4/IPv6 header-length pointer math, and copy the (non-NUL-terminated)
  NFQUEUE payload into a bounded, terminated buffer before the strstr() scans.
- lltdc/src/qospktio.c qos_probe(): the 802.1p reflect path computed the copy
  length against g_txbuf while the source pointer is in g_rxbuf, underflowing
  size_t into an OOB write; measure the offset against g_rxbuf and clamp the
  copy and tx_write length to TXBUFSZ.
- wsdd2/wsd.c: guard the unchecked strstr("\r\n") result (NULL-deref DoS from
  a TCP `POST ` with no CRLF on 3702).
- wsdd2/llmnr.c: bound the LLMNR name label walk and the qtype/qclass reads
  against the received packet (OOB read on UDP 5355).

Verified: full `make rt-be96u` rebuild on the gcc-10.3 toolchain; all 7 files
compile and link with zero new warnings; nand_squashfs image repackaged.
Local branch be96u-only only; never pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
